        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px"><a href="abora">Abora OS</a> is general-purpose Linux distribution based on NixOS. The project's latest release, version 2026.08.28 (also tagged as version 4.0.0 and carrying the codename "Everest"), is available in five desktop editions and introduces non-destructive installs onto an existing partition. "<span class="Quote">Everest ships as five editions: Cosmic, Hyprland, GNOME, KDE Plasma, and Other. The edition controls the live ISO experience, while all 23 supported desktop profiles remain available during installation. The release adds non-destructive installation onto an existing partition, Abora adoption for existing NixOS systems, ANIX v2 with pluggable configuration languages, GPU driver selection for NVIDIA, AMD, and Intel, optional Abora Gaming, a dedicated Abora Gaming Welcome GTK app, TinyPM rewritten in Rust, Linux kernel 7.2, MediaTek MT7902 Wi-Fi 6E and Bluetooth support, and expanded MINT installer support. The App Catalog continues to provide optional Fan Favorites, Essentials, Social, Creator, Developer, Gaming, and System Tools bundles.</span>" Additional information is provided in the distribution's <a href="https://www.aboraos.org/blog/abora-os-v4-everest-coming-soon">release announcement</a>. <a href="https://github.com/AnimatedGTVR/Abora-OS/releases?page=1#release-2026.07.01">Download</a> (<a href="https://github.com/AnimatedGTVR/Abora-OS/releases?page=1#release-2026.07.01">SHA256</a>, <a href="table.php?distribution=abora&pkglist=true&version=2026.08.28#pkglist">pkglist</a>): <a href="https://github.com/AnimatedGTVR/Abora-OS/releases/download/v4.0.0/abora-cosmic-2026.08.28-x86_64-v4.0.iso">abora-cosmic-2026.08.28-x86_64-v4.0.iso</a> (1,940MB), <a href="https://github.com/AnimatedGTVR/Abora-OS/releases/download/v4.0.0/abora-gnome-2026.08.28-x86_64-v4.0.iso">abora-gnome-2026.08.28-x86_64-v4.0.iso</a> (1,940MB), <a href="https://github.com/AnimatedGTVR/Abora-OS/releases/download/v4.0.0/abora